        "answer": {
          "short": "For $x=0,1,2$, the corresponding $y$ values are $\\frac{\\pi}{2},0,-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$. The graph decreases from $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$ through $(1,0)$ to $(2,-\\frac{\\pi}{2})$, with both endpoints included.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y(0)&=\\sin^{-1}(1)=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\\\y(1)&=\\sin^{-1}(0)=0\\\\y(2)&=\\sin^{-1}(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\end{aligned}$$\n\nEnter these values in the table and draw the decreasing inverse sine curve through the three points. Use filled endpoints.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
